# Numra marketing site — Cloudflare Pages redirects
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare Pages rejects absolute-URL sources in _redirects (a
# relative path is required), so the www → apex redirect cannot live
# here. It is handled by attaching both numra-rs.org and
# www.numra-rs.org as custom domains on the same Pages project —
# Pages then issues an automatic 301 from www to apex.
#
# Trailing slash → no trailing slash to align with Astro's
# `trailingSlash: 'never'` config.

# /getting-started → /install (canonical onboarding URL)
/getting-started            /install                     301
/getting-started/*          /install                     301

# Trailing-slash normalization (handled by Astro at build, but fallback)
/install/                   /install                     301
/license/                   /license                     301
/cite/                      /cite                        301
/commercial/                /commercial                  301
/community/                 /community                   301
/stability/                 /stability                   301
/roadmap/                   /roadmap                     301
/changelog/                 /changelog                   301

# 404 fallback (Cloudflare Pages serves /404.html automatically for
# missing pages; no redirect needed, but documented here for clarity).
